<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Legio VII Gemina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">68 CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Legio VII Gemina was a Roman legion raised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galba">Galba</a> in 68 CE. From the reign of Vespasian it was stationed in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> to guard the region and its gold mines, and its camp grew into the city of León, whose name derives from 'legio'. It is attested there into the late Roman period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/legio-vii-gemina.jpg" alt="Legio VII Gemina" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roman_Empire_125.svg: ArdadN derivative work: Richardprins (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iberian_Peninsula_in_125-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
